Sprocket here! That sounds like a super fun project! Let's break it down like building a LEGO castle — one piece at a time.

### Step 1: Start with the HTML
HTML is like the skeleton of your webpage. It tells the browser what to show. Let's make a simple structure for your quiz.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>Quiz Game</title>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>My Quiz Game</h1>
  <div id="quiz"></div>
  <button onclick="nextQuestion()">Next Question</button>
  <script src="quiz.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

### Step 2: Add some JavaScript
JavaScript is like the brain of your game — it makes things happen! Let's create a simple quiz with one question.

Create a file called `quiz.js` and add this:

```javascript
let currentQuestion = 0;
const questions = [
  {
    question: "What is the capital of France?",
    options: ["Paris", "London", "Berlin", "Madrid"],
    answer: "Paris"
  }
];

function nextQuestion() {
  const questionDiv = document.getElementById("quiz");
  questionDiv.innerHTML = "";

  const current = questions[currentQuestion];
  const questionText = document.createElement("p");
  questionText.textContent = current.question;
  questionDiv.appendChild(questionText);

  current.options.forEach(option => {
    const button = document.createElement("button");
    button.textContent = option;
    button.onclick = () => checkAnswer(option);
    questionDiv.appendChild(button);
  });
}

function checkAnswer(selected) {
  const current = questions[currentQuestion];
  if (selected === current.answer) {
    alert("Correct!");
  } else {
    alert("Wrong! The correct answer is " + current.answer);
  }

  currentQuestion++;
  if (currentQuestion < questions.length) {
    nextQuestion();
  } else {
    alert("Quiz complete!");
  }
}
```

### Step 3: Add some style (optional)
You can make it look nicer with a little CSS. Add this inside the `<head>` of your HTML:

```html
<style>
  body {
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    text-align: center;
    padding: 20px;
  }
  button {
    margin: 10px;
    padding: 10px 20px;
    font-size: 16px;
  }
</style>
```

### What's Next?
- You can add more questions to the `questions` array.
- You can add a score tracker.
- You can make it multiple choice with radio buttons or checkboxes.

