To pin a Terraform provider version across all your modules without editing each one manually, you can use a **Terraform module version constraint** in your root `terraform.tfversion` file and use a **shared provider configuration** in your root module.

### Step-by-step:

1. **Set a Terraform version in `terraform.tfversion`** (top-level):
   ```hcl
   terraform {
     required_version = ">= 1.5.0"
   }
   ```

2. **Define a provider version constraint in your root module** (e.g., `main.tf`):
   ```hcl
   terraform {
     required_providers {
       aws = {
         source  = "hashicorp/aws"
         version = ">= 5.0.0"
       }
     }
   }
   ```

3. **Ensure all modules use the same provider source** (e.g., in `modules/your-module/versions.tf`):
   ```hcl
   provider "aws" {
     source = "hashicorp/aws"
   }
   ```

This ensures that all modules use the same provider version, and Terraform will enforce it during plan and apply.

> 📌 For more details, see the [Terraform documentation on provider version constraints](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/providers/requirements).

